  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "ps_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -324
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Slingshot Sandbox\n\nPress anywhere, pull back and let go: a ball flies from where you pressed, opposite the pull, like a slingshot — the dotted arc shows where it will go. G cycles gravity (down, none, up), W switches the walls between bouncing and wrapping round, C clears the balls, R turns the rain of balls from the top on and off. Balls bounce off the bumpers.\n\nHow it works: one Emitter launches a ball on the frame you let go (rate 61/s for one 1/60 s frame = one ball) with the pull as its velocity, and on rain ticks drops one at the top. Three Worlds share the bumpers: a bouncing one, a wrapping one and a 'kill' one the Emitter is handed for a single frame to clear.",
        "width": 460,
        "height": 260
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ps_mouse",
      "defType": "input/mouse",
      "position": {
